        "raw": "<p>My daughter, Cheekers, and I just finished our first game of Fate of the Elder Gods this evening.<span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">It came down to the wire.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">She picked Cthulhu and I randomly dealt myself Hastur. I was up for most of the game due to&nbsp;</span><em style=\"font-size: 13px;\">very</em><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\"> lucky rolls (5/6 and 3/5) on the Other Worlds that I was contantly feeding through the Gathering. She was going very heavy on readying spells, which was preventing me from managing to ready much of anything. </span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">So, there I was with a <em>&#39;An Ancient Stirring&#39;</em> in my hand from the start of the game that would win me the game, but unable to cast because I never arranged the spell cards correctly. However, I had a cultist on Other Worlds and an artifact that let me flip the die face to the opposite side by sacrificing a cultist. Meanwhile, Cheekers was on the summoning track at seven but had some unfortunate luck with the acursed investigators and had nine out of ten Elder Signs. She was also cursed because on the previous round her marker met up with the Elder Signs. Which curse you ask? The one that triggers when you remove an Elder SIgn, cancels that removal, and </span><em style=\"font-size: 13px;\">adds</em><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\"> one more Elder Sign. </span><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Basically, I couldn&#39;t lose.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">On her turn Cheekers tells me she&#39;s casting a spell.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">It&#39;s <em>&#39;An Ancient Stirring&#39;</em>. She goes up one one her summon track and then sacrifices a cultist to go up one more to nine and win the game. ...With the card I&#39;ve been trying to play the whole game. I&#39;m so proud.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Fhtagn.</span></p>",
